 ### Linearly Annealed Dropout (LAD)
-A regularization technique that applies strong stochastic masking in early training to disrupt premature primitive co-adaptation, then linearly decays the dropout probability to zero to restore full capacity for structural consolidation [S1, unofficial]. Choose when early view-specific co-adaptation is a primary concern. See [Linearly Annealed Dropout](17550-linearly-annealed-dropout.md).
