 ### Structure-Aware Early Stopping (SAES)
-A stopping criterion that monitors Gaussian population growth momentum to detect structural saturation and terminates densification without ground-truth metrics [S1, unofficial]. Choose when volumetric fidelity degradation due to redundant late-stage densification is observed. See [Structure-Aware Early Stopping](17551-structure-aware-early-stopping.md).
